# Epistemology and the Socio-Cognitive Perspective in Information Science.

**Authors:** Hjorland, Birger

## Abstract
Presents a socio-cognitive perspective in relation to information science and information retrieval. Topics include differences between traditional cognitive views and socio-cognitive views; a comparison of behaviorism, cognitivism, psychoanalysis, and neuroscience as approaches in psychology; information needs; relevance criteria; and epistemology and information science. (Author/LRW)

